===Etymology 1===
{{suffix|en|groove|y}}

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|er}}

# Of, pertaining to, or having [[groove]]s.
#: ''The back of the tile was '''groovy''' so that it could hold the adhesive compound.''
# {{lb|en|dated}} Set in one's ways.
#* {{w|Rudyard Kipling}}
#*: She'd give anything to be able to believe it, but she's a hard woman, and brooding along certain lines makes one '''groovy'''.

===Etymology 2===
From the phrase {{m|en|in the groove}}, originally in reference to the grooves of an early phonograph record.

